Task 1: Create Smart Inventories Based on Labels or Tags
Subtask 1.1: Understanding Smart Inventories
Smart Inventories in RHACM are dynamic collections of managed clusters that automatically update based on defined criteria such as labels, annotations, or cluster properties.

Key Benefits:

Dynamic Management: Automatically include/exclude clusters based on changing criteria
Scalability: Manage hundreds of clusters efficiently
Consistency: Apply policies uniformly across similar cluster groups
Automation: Reduce manual cluster grouping tasks
Subtask 1.2: Access RHACM Console
Open your web browser and navigate to the RHACM console
Log in with your provided credentials
Navigate to Infrastructure → Clusters to view your managed clusters
# Verify cluster access via CLI
oc get managedclusters
Subtask 1.3: Examine Existing Cluster Labels
Before creating smart inventories, examine the labels on your managed clusters:

# List all managed clusters with their labels
oc get managedclusters --show-labels

# Get detailed information about a specific cluster
oc describe managedcluster <cluster-name>
Subtask 1.4: Add Labels to Managed Clusters
Add meaningful labels to your clusters for smart inventory grouping:

# Add environment label to clusters
oc label managedcluster cluster1 environment=production
oc label managedcluster cluster2 environment=development
oc label managedcluster cluster3 environment=staging

# Add region labels
oc label managedcluster cluster1 region=us-east
oc label managedcluster cluster2 region=us-west
oc label managedcluster cluster3 region=eu-central

# Add cluster type labels
oc label managedcluster cluster1 cluster-type=compute
oc label managedcluster cluster2 cluster-type=edge
