Subtask 1.5: Create Your First Smart Inventory
Create a smart inventory for production clusters:

# Create file: production-smart-inventory.yaml
apiVersion: cluster.open-cluster-management.io/v1beta1
kind: ManagedClusterSet
metadata:
  name: production-clusters
  labels:
    inventory-type: smart
    environment: production
spec:
  clusterSelector:
    selectorType: ExclusiveClusterSetLabel
---
apiVersion: cluster.open-cluster-management.io/v1beta1
kind: ManagedClusterSetBinding
metadata:
  name: production-clusters-binding
  namespace: default
spec:
  clusterSet: production-clusters
Apply the smart inventory:

# Apply the smart inventory configuration
oc apply -f production-smart-inventory.yaml

# Verify the smart inventory was created
oc get managedclustersets
Subtask 1.6: Create Region-Based Smart Inventory
Create a smart inventory for US-based clusters:

# Create file: us-region-smart-inventory.yaml
apiVersion: cluster.open-cluster-management.io/v1beta1
kind: ManagedClusterSet
metadata:
  name: us-region-clusters
  labels:
    inventory-type: smart
    region: us
spec:
  clusterSelector:
    selectorType: LabelSelector
    labelSelector:
      matchExpressions:
      - key: region
        operator: In
        values:
        - us-east
        - us-west
---
apiVersion: cluster.open-cluster-management.io/v1beta1
kind: ManagedClusterSetBinding
metadata:
  name: us-region-clusters-binding
  namespace: default
spec:
  clusterSet: us-region-clusters
# Apply the region-based smart inventory
oc apply -f us-region-smart-inventory.yaml

# Verify clusters are automatically included
oc get managedclusters -l 'region in (us-east,us-west)'
Subtask 1.7: Create Complex Smart Inventory with Multiple Criteria
Create a smart inventory combining multiple criteria:

# Create file: complex-smart-inventory.yaml
apiVersion: cluster.open-cluster-management.io/v1beta1
kind: ManagedClusterSet
metadata:
  name: production-compute-clusters
  labels:
    inventory-type: smart
    purpose: high-performance
spec:
  clusterSelector:
    selectorType: LabelSelector
    labelSelector:
      matchLabels:
        environment: production
        cluster-type: compute
      matchExpressions:
      - key: region
        operator: In
        values:
        - us-east
        - eu-central
# Apply the complex smart inventory
oc apply -f complex-smart-inventory.yaml

# Verify the selection criteria
oc get managedclusters -l environment=production,cluster-type=compute
Task 2: Use Smart Inventories for Policy and Resource Management
Subtask 2.1: Create Governance Policies for Smart Inventories
Create a security policy that applies to production clusters:

# Create file: production-security-policy.yaml
apiVersion: policy.open-cluster-management.io/v1
kind: Policy
metadata:
  name: production-security-policy
  namespace: default
  annotations:
    policy.open-cluster-management.io/standards: NIST-CSF
    policy.open-cluster-management.io/categories: PR.AC Access Control
    policy.open-cluster-management.io/controls: PR.AC-4
spec:
  remediationAction: enforce
  disabled: false
  policy-templates:
    - objectDefinition:
        apiVersion: policy.open-cluster-management.io/v1
        kind: ConfigurationPolicy
        metadata:
          name: production-pod-security-policy
        spec:
          remediationAction: enforce
          severity: high
          namespaceSelector:
            exclude:
            - kube-*
            - openshift-*
          object-templates:
            - complianceType: musthave
              objectDefinition:
                apiVersion: v1
                kind: LimitRange
                metadata:
                  name: production-limits
                spec:
                  limits:
                  - default:
                      cpu: "1"
                      memory: "1Gi"
                    defaultRequest:
                      cpu: "0.1"
                      memory: "128Mi"
                    type: Container
---
apiVersion: policy.open-cluster-management.io/v1
kind: PlacementBinding
metadata:
  name: production-security-policy-binding
  namespace: default
spec:
  bindingOverrides:
    remediationAction: enforce
  placementRef:
    name: production-clusters-placement
    kind: PlacementRule
    apiGroup: apps.open-cluster-management.io
  subjects:
  - name: production-security-policy
    kind: Policy
    apiGroup: policy.open-cluster-management.io
---
apiVersion: apps.open-cluster-management.io/v1
kind: PlacementRule
metadata:
  name: production-clusters-placement
  namespace: default
spec:
  clusterSelector:
    matchLabels:
      environment: production
Subtask 2.2: Apply Policy to Smart Inventory
# Apply the production security policy
oc apply -f production-security-policy.yaml

# Verify policy creation
oc get policies -n default

# Check policy status
oc describe policy production-security-policy -n default
Subtask 2.3: Create Application Deployment Using Smart Inventories
Create an application that deploys only to development clusters:

# Create file: dev-app-deployment.yaml
apiVersion: argoproj.io/v1alpha1
kind: Application
metadata:
  name: dev-sample-app
  namespace: argocd
spec:
  project: default
  source:
    repoURL: https://github.com/argoproj/argocd-example-apps.git
    targetRevision: HEAD
    path: guestbook
  destination:
    server: https://kubernetes.default.svc
    namespace: guestbook
  syncPolicy:
    automated:
      prune: true
      selfHeal: true
---
apiVersion: apps.open-cluster-management.io/v1
kind: PlacementRule
metadata:
  name: dev-clusters-placement
  namespace: argocd
spec:
  clusterSelector:
    matchLabels:
      environment: development
Subtask 2.4: Create Resource Quotas for Smart Inventories
Apply different resource quotas based on cluster types:

# Create file: cluster-resource-quotas.yaml
apiVersion: policy.open-cluster-management.io/v1
kind: Policy
metadata:
  name: compute-cluster-quotas
  namespace: default
spec:
  remediationAction: enforce
  disabled: false
  policy-templates:
    - objectDefinition:
        apiVersion: policy.open-cluster-management.io/v1
        kind: ConfigurationPolicy
        metadata:
          name: compute-resource-quota
        spec:
          remediationAction: enforce
          severity: medium
          namespaceSelector:
            include:
            - default
          object-templates:
            - complianceType: musthave
              objectDefinition:
                apiVersion: v1
                kind: ResourceQuota
                metadata:
                  name: compute-cluster-quota
                spec:
                  hard:
                    requests.cpu: "100"
                    requests.memory: "200Gi"
                    limits.cpu: "200"
                    limits.memory: "400Gi"
                    persistentvolumeclaims: "50"
---
apiVersion: apps.open-cluster-management.io/v1
kind: PlacementRule
metadata:
  name: compute-clusters-placement
  namespace: default
spec:
  clusterSelector:
    matchLabels:
      cluster-type: compute
# Apply resource quota policy
oc apply -f cluster-resource-quotas.yaml

# Monitor policy compliance
oc get policies -n default
